## Part 5 — The §4a reword window: the cost figure in plan §4 is overtaken

Plan §4 quantifies the decision as **"9 commits to reword now vs 16 later."** Measured at the actual
tip: **11 of 17 commit messages carry a plans-branch token.** The "now" price has already risen from
9 to 11, and C11/C10/C9 will push it toward 14. The time-box has been partly spent while the
decision sat open — that is the substance of the update Dean needs, and it does not change the
recommendation either way, only the number attached to it.

Token-carrying messages: `4fb49ac6`, `537b0153`, `a679f2ad` (C6f), `784c2b5c` (C6e), `330fcd26`
(C6d), `1140a4c2`, `952d2fff`, `3c9d45bb` (Bug #3), `07b8fdb7` (Bug #1), `50034d15` (Bug #2),
`b106b929`, `680bebdb` (N2). Clean: `eb12089a`, `a46c7eea`, `34b18bc5`, `d9f3b97e`, `8eb6ee2d`.

**In-tree comment debt also grew, and the plan's recorded figure is not comparable.** Counting
genuine plans tokens only (`N1-9`, `W1-5`, `U1-5`, `C2`/`C6x`/`C7`/`C11`, `PR-1|2`) in
`internal/engines/pipeline/*.go`:

| ref | lines |
|---|---|
| `075a208e` (PR-1 base) | 1 |
| `d9f3b97e` (plan's measurement point) | 22 |
| `eb12089a` (current tip) | **36** |

It nearly doubled across C6c–C6f. Note `4fb49ac6` removed plans-branch *paths*, not section tokens,
so that commit does not discharge this.

**Caveat you should resolve before quoting either number:** the plan records "48 in-tree at
`d9f3b97e`, of which 31 are PR-2's and 17 already present at the PR-1 base `075a208e`". My tighter
filter gives **1** inherited, not 17 — because the plan's grep also catches real code identifiers:
golden-scenario names (`A1`–`A4`, `C1`, `V1`) and the `T1-ols` reason string, which are legitimate
and must not be renamed. The two figures are therefore not comparable, and the "17 inherited, out of
scope" share looks considerably smaller than recorded — meaning **more of the debt is PR-2's own than
the plan currently credits.** Pin one agreed grep expression in the plan and re-measure at the
current tip; C9 is the host either way, but its scope is larger than the plan says.

